---
// Policies: the index of every policy, with a short summary of each (src/lib/info.ts POLICIES).
// Two are written with the Code ↔ Paper reader, on another branch (/policies/code/,
// /policies/moderation/): linked once they exist, named until then.
import Info from "../../components/Info.astro";
import { SITE_NAME } from "../../config";
import { pageExists, POLICIES } from "../../lib/info";
import { REVIEW_DAYS } from "../../lib/moderation";
---
<Info
  title="Policies"
  description={`${SITE_NAME}'s policies: licences and statements, the authors' code, the paper's full text, removals, moderation, DOIs, privacy, terms, conduct, accessibility, citation.`}
  group="policies"
  path="/policies/"
>
  <p class="lead" slot="lead">
    The rules {SITE_NAME} holds itself to, each in its own page: what it shows and copies, what it never does, how it
    decides what people ask of it, and what it asks of them. They describe how the registry's code actually behaves;
    when one changes, its page says so.
  </p>

  <dl class="index">
    {POLICIES.map((l) => (
      <>
        <dt>{pageExists(l.href) ? <a href={l.href}>{l.text}</a> : <>{l.text} <span class="muted">(to be published)</span></>}</dt>
        <dd>{l.summary}</dd>
      </>
    ))}
  </dl>

  <h2 id="principles">The principles behind them</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>The source prevails.</strong> The registry records and links; the paper and the repository are the
      reference.</li>
    <li><strong>Licences first.</strong> Nothing is copied or reproduced beyond what its licence allows: code whose
      licence allows no copy is shown from its source by the reader's browser, never from a copy.</li>
    <li><strong>No email address</strong> is asked for, shown or needed to use any part of the registry.</li>
    <li><strong>Published rules decide</strong> what people ask, in the safe direction: hiding is automatic when in
      doubt, publishing needs a verified identity or checks that pass. The operator reviews what the rules cannot
      decide, can reverse what they did, and nothing waits more than {REVIEW_DAYS} days — except a request about personal
      data, which the operator answers within one month, and which is never closed unanswered.</li>
    <li><strong>Zero cost</strong>, for readers and for the registry: no fee, no advertising, no tracking.</li>
  </ul>
</Info>
